<statement>
<p>
Fill in the missing pieces in the conversion of the decimal integer <m>\displaystyle{\left({53}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> into its binary (base-2) representation.
</p>
<p>
53 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(26) + 1</p>
<p>
26 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(13) + 0</p>
<p>
13 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(6) + 1</p>
<p>
6 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(3) + 0</p>
<p>
3 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(1) + 1</p>
<p>
1 = <fillin characters="1" /><asterisk/>(0) + 1
</p>
<p>
The binary representation of <m>\displaystyle{\left({53}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> is <m>\displaystyle{(}</m><fillin characters="1" /><m>\displaystyle{)}_{{{2}}}</m>

</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p><ul><li>2</li><li>2</li><li>2</li><li>2</li><li>2</li><li>2</li><li>110101</li></ul></p>
</solution>
